   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to prohibiting\ncertain uses of trichloroethylene; and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2020,\namending the environmental conservation law relating to prohibiting certain\nuses of trichloroethylene, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 6829-B\nand A. 8829-A, in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S902",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S902-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §37-0119, En Con L; amd §2, Chap of 2020 (as proposed in S.6829-B & A.8829-A)",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S902\n\nSPONSOR: KAMINSKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nprohibiting certain uses of trichloroethylene; and to amend a chapter of\nthe laws of 2020, amending the environmental conservation law relating\nto prohibiting certain uses of trichloroethylene, as proposed in legis-\nlative bills numbers S. 6829-B and A. 8829-A, in relation to the effec-\ntiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2020,\nc.370.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by delaying the effective\ndate of the prohibition of certain uses of trichloroethylene (TCE) by\none year and adding a severability clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 66 of 2020, the Executive stated that a delay\nin the effective date was needed in order to provide additional time for\nthe identification of safe and effective alternatives to TCE and that\naddition of a severability clause was necessary to protect against\npossible preemption from regulatory action by the United States Environ-\nmental Protection Agency. This legislation is a negotiated change to the\nunderlying chapter that addresses those concerns.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 370 of the Laws of 2020.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect December 1, 2022.\n",
